      "THOMASIN: Or perchance I’ll boil and bake thee since we are lack of food.\nMERCY: Stop!",
      "KATHERINE: Thomasin, where hast thou put the silver cup?\nTHOMASIN: Is’t not on the shelf?\nKATHERINE: Nay.\nTHOMASIN: In the six board then.",
      "KATHERINE: Enough.\nTHOMASIN: I promised.\nKATHERINE: I care not.\nTHOMASIN: Let me find favor in your eyes."
    ]
